+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Voyage 1: TodoMVC build
+
+**Goal:** Implement a Vanilla JS TodoMVC app per `assets/app-spec.md`, using `assets/app-template.index.html` as base markup. Persist to `localStorage`.
+
+**Stack:** Vanilla JavaScript, no preprocessors. Cucumber + happy-dom for verification (already installed). `todomvc-common` and `todomvc-app-css` referenced from `node_modules/` (installed but gitignored).
+
+**Specs authored:**
+- `features/adding-todos.feature` -- 7 scenarios: create, trim, empty guard, focus, multi-add
+- `features/toggling-todos.feature` -- 3 scenarios: complete, uncomplete, toggle-all reflection
+- `features/mark-all.feature` -- 4 scenarios: mark all, unmark all, toggle-all checked/unchecked sync
+- `features/editing-todos.feature` -- 7 scenarios: double-click, save on Enter/blur, discard on Escape, empty-delete, trim, class removal
+- `features/filtering-todos.feature` -- 5 scenarios: all/active/completed routes, toggle-in-filter hides, selected link
+- `features/clear-completed.feature` -- 3 scenarios: clear action, button hidden/visible
+- `features/persistence.feature` -- 4 scenarios: persist, completed state, order, no editing-mode persist
+- `features/counter-and-visibility.feature` -- 8 scenarios: counter plural/singular/zero, update on toggle, section visibility, strong tag
+
+**Total: 41 product-lane scenarios across 8 features.**
+
+**Watchbill:** 8 watches ordered by dependency. watch1 (add) first, then toggle, mark-all, counter/visibility, editing, clear-completed, filtering (needs routing), persistence (needs reload support).
+
+**Harness:** `features/support/world.js` loads real `index.html` + `js/app.js` via happy-dom. Provides `this.document`, `this.window`, `this.navigate(hash)`, `this.localStorage`. Fires `DOMContentLoaded` and `load` events. Patches `hashchange` dispatch on click. Disposes per scenario.
+
+**Open questions:**
+- RIGGING.md not yet derived (Shipwright's job at fitting out).
+- No production code exists yet. `index.html` and `js/app.js` must be created before verification can run.
+
+**Next role:** QM dispatch. Requires: (1) RIGGING.md derived by Shipwright, (2) production artifacts (`index.html`, `js/app.js`, `css/app.css`) created by Crew through QM dispatch.
