@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+Feature: Counter and section visibility
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want the item count to reflect my active todos
+  And I want the app sections to appear only when relevant
+  So that I have clear feedback about my task list state
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows the number of active items
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    Then the counter shows "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter singular form for one item
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter zero items
+    Then the counter shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter updates when an item is completed
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter updates when an item is toggled back to active
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has completed the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the counter shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Main section and footer are hidden when there are no todos
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer section is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Main section and footer are visible when there are todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the main section is visible
+    And the footer section is visible
+
+  Scenario: The strong tag wraps the counter number
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the counter number "1" is wrapped in a strong tag
diff --git a/features/editing-todos.feature b/features/editing-todos.feature
