+++ b/features/filtering-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+Feature: Filtering todos
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want to filter my todos by completion status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: All filter shows all todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has completed the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user navigates to "#/"
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only incomplete todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has completed the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the visible todo has title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has completed the todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the visible todo has title "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo in a filtered view hides it appropriately
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the visible todo has title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: The selected filter link reflects the current route
+    When the user navigates to "#/"
+    Then the "All" filter is selected
+    When the user navigates to "#/active"
+    Then the "Active" filter is selected
+    When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+    Then the "Completed" filter is selected
diff --git a/features/mark-all.feature b/features/mark-all.feature
