--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+Feature: Persistence
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want my todos to be saved when I close the browser
+  So that I can resume my task list later
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Todos are persisted to localStorage
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Buy milk" and is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Completed state is persisted
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has completed the todo "Buy milk"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+
+  Scenario: Multiple todos are persisted in order
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    And the user has added a todo "Walk the dog"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains 2 items
+    And the first todo has title "Buy milk" and is not completed
+    And the second todo has title "Walk the dog" and is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted
+    Given the user has added a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk" label
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is not in editing mode
